<section id="S4" class="ltx_section">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_section"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_section">4 </span>Computing Plane Star-Forest Decompositions on Small Point Sets</h2>

<div id="S4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Using a simple computer search, we managed to find all point sets on <math id="S4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="6" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>6</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">6</annotation></semantics></math> points that can be decomposed into <math id="S4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="4" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>4</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">4</annotation></semantics></math> plane star-forests and all point sets on <math id="S4.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="8" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>8</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">8</annotation></semantics></math> points that can be decomposed into <math id="S4.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="5" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>5</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">5</annotation></semantics></math> plane star-forests. Out of the <math id="S4.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="16" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>16</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">16</annotation></semantics></math> order types on <math id="S4.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="6" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>6</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">6</annotation></semantics></math> points, which can be found on <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib1" title="" class="ltx_ref">1</a>]</cite>, we have found decompositions which satisfy the requirements from Theorem <a href="#S3.Thmtheorem1" title="Theorem 3.1 ‣ 3 Decomposing Complete Geometric Graphs into Plane Star-Forests ‣ Star-Forest Decompositions of Complete Graphs" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.1</span></a> for <math id="S4.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="6" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>6</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">6</annotation></semantics></math> of them. Those point sets and corresponding partitions can be seen in Figure <a href="#S4.F6" title="Figure 6 ‣ 4 Computing Plane Star-Forest Decompositions on Small Point Sets ‣ Star-Forest Decompositions of Complete Graphs" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">6</span></a>. Out of <math id="S4.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="3315" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>3315</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">3315</annotation></semantics></math> order types on <math id="S4.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="8" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>8</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">8</annotation></semantics></math> points, we have found such decompositions for <math id="S4.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="411" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>411</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">411</annotation></semantics></math> of them.
The code is available at <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib4" title="" class="ltx_ref">4</a>]</cite>. We plan to continue improving the code to be able to perform the search on bigger point sets. Currently, the generation of appropriate decompositions is very slow, and since the number of edges and corresponding decompositions grows very fast, we are not able to perform the checks for bigger point sets. Of course, for even bigger point sets, a completely different approach would be needed, as the number of different order types for <math id="S4.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n\geq 12" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>12</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n\geq 12</annotation></semantics></math> becomes too large to handle. For this, using SAT solvers might be useful to try and resolve Conjectures <a href="#Thmconjecture2" title="Conjecture 2 ‣ 3 Decomposing Complete Geometric Graphs into Plane Star-Forests ‣ Star-Forest Decompositions of Complete Graphs" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a> and <a href="#Thmconjecture3" title="Conjecture 3 ‣ 3 Decomposing Complete Geometric Graphs into Plane Star-Forests ‣ Star-Forest Decompositions of Complete Graphs" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a>.</p>
</div>
